Design a one-bit full adder circuit. It takes three inputs: two significant bits (bit0 and bit1) and a carry-in (cin). The module outputs a sum bit and a carry-out (cout). The sum is computed as the XOR of the three input bits, while the carry-out is determined by the majority function of the inputs, indicating whether a carry is generated when adding the two bits along with the incoming carry.
module top_module(input bit0, bit1, cin,
                  output sum, cout);

