description:
Design a 3-to-8 line decoder. The circuit takes a 3-bit input and activates one of the eight output lines based on the binary value of the input. For each unique 3-bit input value from 000 to 111, one corresponding output line will go HIGH, while all others will remain LOW, providing a simple way to decode 3-bit values into a single active output.
module top_module(
  input [2:0] in,
  output [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [2:0] in,
  output [7:0] out
);reg [7:0] out_reg;

  always @(*) begin
    case(in)
      3'b000: out_reg = 8'b00000001;
      3'b001: out_reg = 8'b00000010;
      3'b010: out_reg = 8'b00000100;
      3'b011: out_reg = 8'b00001000;
      3'b100: out_reg = 8'b00010000;
      3'b101: out_reg = 8'b00100000;
      3'b110: out_reg = 8'b01000000;
      3'b111: out_reg = 8'b10000000;
      default: out_reg = 8'b00000000;
    endcase
  end

  assign out = out_reg;

endmodule

