description:
Design a circuit to compute the parity of a single-bit input. It maintains a two-bit counter to track the number of ones received, updating the count with each input. The output indicates the parity, where a LOW output signifies an even number of ones and a HIGH output signifies an odd number.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);reg [1:0] count;

  always @ (in) begin
    count = {count[0], in} + count[1];
  end

  assign out = ~count[0];

endmodule

