description:
Design a circuit that performs a 4x4 matrix multiplication. The module takes two 16-bit input vectors, A and B, representing two 4x4 matrices, and outputs a 16-bit vector C, which contains the resulting matrix after multiplication. The implementation utilizes nested loops to iterate through the matrix rows and columns, accumulating products of corresponding elements from A and B into the output matrix C.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] A,
    input [15:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] C
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] A,
    input [15:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] C
);integer i, j, k;
    reg [15:0] temp;

    always @(*) begin
        // Initialize the output matrix C to zero
        C = 0;

        for(i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
            for(j = 0; j < 4; j = j + 1) begin
                temp = 0;
                for(k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) begin
                    temp = temp + A[i*4 + k] * B[k*4 + j];
                end
                C[i*4 + j] = temp; // Corrected to assign temp to the specific index.
            end
        end
    end

endmodule

